## Necessary proof cases and currently missing prerequisites
Required actual privileged positives: direct retained protected helper creates before-exec realm and root-family; original nonroot sudo apt transition installs actual verified DEB in its realm; original same-realm dpkg/version/ELF/desktop/icon/ldd checks and nonroot GUI work; AppImage real installed-start acceptance; ordinary source/read/controller mismatch rejects before effects. Required native negatives: launcher inode/ELF/dependency substitution, native elevation denial, cgroup creation or clone3 placement failure, bad uidmap/capreadback, inherited ancestor FD, service-manager endpoint, escaped grandchild/IO, worker overflow/protocol reorder, cancellation while setup/install/teardown, package-input replacement, reap/close/unmount failure. Preserve native attempted test IDs and raw observations on every exit; skip/xfail/JSON completion cannot supply PASS.

Missing current facts: trusted-bootstrap directly created coordinator/held activation issuer, protected dedicated-host-UID loader/import isolation with no dumpable-reset window, native one-use restart exclusion, protected helper bytes/compiler/load identity, actualCI nosuid/elevation/cgroup/clone3 permissions, fresh mutually exclusive host-ID range, signed seed package identities/dependency closure, exact package maintainers' capability compatibility, actual runtime/GUI identities and native complete family retirement. These are explicit prerequisites for future disposable-CI execution; the design has implemented none. Final0.7 candidate, five install slots, tag/server conditions and publication native authority remain unfinished. PR98 cancellation and Issue86 snapshot pause are unchanged.
